    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.pick, mini.extra\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nHi echasnovski! Is it in scope to add pickers to leverage nvim-dap functionality to toggle breakpoints, scopes and frames to mini.extra just like how fzf-lua does with commands like `dap_breakpoints`, `dap_variables` and `dap_frames`. And if you are ok with including these in mini.extra and are ok with me contributing, I can probably try raising a PR for these pickers if can get them to work to mini.extra.",
